Package: tidyview
Title: Guided Data Workflow GUI with Paste-Ready R Code
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Elmer", "Tumlos", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "e.tumlos@psa.gov.ph")
Author: Elmer Tumlos [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Elmer Tumlos <e.tumlos@psa.gov.ph>
Description: A Material Design 3 graphical user interface for guided data
    workflows with a tidyverse-style interface and a data.table execution
    engine. Provides a browser-based GUI launched via tidygui() that lets
    users inspect, audit, validate, filter, select, mutate, summarise,
    join, reshape, tabulate, compare, and export data frames using
    point-and-click interactions. The interface is designed to be teachable
    and non-technical-user friendly, with plain-language labels, safer
    previews before destructive actions, and generated paste-ready R code
    displayed live in a code pane. Supports loading data from the R
    environment, CSV, TSV, Excel, RDS, RCDF, and other R-compatible
    formats, including list-column datasets such as dplyr::starwars.
